# Configuration System

The application uses YAML-based configuration files to define crew behavior.

## Configuration Directories

Each crew type has its own configuration directory:

- [src/report_generation/config/health_history/](mdc:src/report_generation/config/health_history): Health history crew config
- [src/report_generation/config/health_live/](mdc:src/report_generation/config/health_live): Health live crew config
- [src/report_generation/config/youtube_history/](mdc:src/report_generation/config/youtube_history): YouTube history crew config
- [src/report_generation/config/youtube_live/](mdc:src/report_generation/config/youtube_live): YouTube live crew config

## Configuration Files

Each configuration directory contains two main files:

1. `agents.yaml`: Defines the agents in a crew (roles, goals, backstories)
2. `tasks.yaml`: Defines the tasks for each agent (description, expected output)

## Environment Variables

The application also uses environment variables for API keys and other settings:

- [.env](mdc:.env): Environment variable file
- Main variable: `OPENAI_API_KEY` for accessing OpenAI's API

